Name data sources
=================

names_data.go contains a compact selection of given and family names from:

- faker-js/faker v10.1.0, commit f81abc77a34d8a2016f06b73ed859fef44446c2d
  https://github.com/faker-js/faker/tree/f81abc77a34d8a2016f06b73ed859fef44446c2d/src/locales
  src/locales/<locale>/person/first_name.ts and last_name.ts for:
  af_ZA, de, en, en_IN, en_NG, es, fi, fr, it, nl, pt_BR, ro, tr.
- joke2k/faker v37.12.0, commit 949a8d6ff538b86a6a40b2082beaeade480e891a
  https://github.com/joke2k/faker/tree/949a8d6ff538b86a6a40b2082beaeade480e891a/faker/providers/person
  en_PK/__init__.py first_names and last_names; ja_JP/__init__.py
  first_name_female_pairs, first_name_male_pairs, and last_name_pairs
  (the upstream romanized forms); vi_VN/__init__.py first_names_female,
  first_names_unisex, first_names_male, and last_names.

Names are lowercased and Latin accents are removed. Latin letters not handled
by Unicode decomposition use these substitutions: i for dotless i, ss for
eszett, ae for ae ligature, o for o with stroke, l for l with stroke, d for
d with stroke and eth, and th for thorn. Only single names of 2-10 ASCII
letters are retained. Each locale contributes at most 64 given and 64 family
names. Selection ranks normalized values by SHA-256, then sorts each selected
list alphabetically. Given names are disjoint across pools: allocate locales
in ascending available given-name count (locale breaks ties), excluding names
already allocated to a previous pool. Family names stay within their locale.

The catalog contains 16 locales and 56,428 distinct name pairs.
The runtime uses only these static lists, with no Faker dependency or download.

